[{"id":"VRCE-1-25-1","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":25,"verse":1,"english":"Hearing those bold words of the ascetic, the son of that foremost of men, Rāghava firm in his vows, with clasped hands answered.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-26-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1025001","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5402320a486ff876569a1bdd4537c95cd89a0813b0a314cfb46f70e77db981b9","compact":"4c24d66471365517d6e763501a3021d909b6316fa71af2b065bb717ae9595884","nasal":"20bb265964f8539d89dbe02218e0f70bfe2b1eb6150b2bfcb3f44989c121c9ad"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-25-2","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":25,"verse":2,"english":"In accordance with the desire of my sire, and in order to glorify it, I ought fearlessly to do even as Kusika's son says. And having been desired to that end while at Ayodhyā by that high-souled one, my father Dasaratha, in the midst of the spiritual guides, I ought not to pass by your words.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-26-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1025002","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ada02caa751242f0e1fcf15e842c0cf2cee3f2523e08e37890e12f03f169bd38","compact":"2d734cdbb3b9c9d74bcb3e35bd3955118a9789a8223b78a9d698ffc310d00ece","nasal":"8192d5d8e0f5806926d127e47e6dfb2b833776d75cf0288bd2cb55034e2929a5"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-25-3","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":25,"verse":3,"english":"In accordance with the desire of my sire, and in order to glorify it, I ought fearlessly to do even as Kusika's son says. And having been desired to that end while at Ayodhyā by that high-souled one, my father Dasaratha, in the midst of the spiritual guides, I ought not to pass by your words.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.891,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-26-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1025003","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7f2d23a1f03236c90b8c6226dccea2bc8e4f3a2a9d2602f6410d27b41de54f59","compact":"50fb16e1862f956a0b3f6986c4e89cf8928322ef171b6efc6787fefde2f9951f","nasal":"50fb16e1862f956a0b3f6986c4e89cf8928322ef171b6efc6787fefde2f9951f"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-25-4","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":25,"verse":4,"english":"Therefore, commanded by that upholder of the Veda, I, agreeably to my father's mandate, will, without doubt, bring about that welcome event-the death of Tataka.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-26-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1025004","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f34d35e356c5bd262f46b5f5399e2c8b3c212b31939d6d4dcfbf1ec188cc7d30","compact":"eda13290f616ee95ce17cc92eb6e3cb1ef4621f2f094d56d90a68a55ead36b01","nasal":"eda13290f616ee95ce17cc92eb6e3cb1ef4621f2f094d56d90a68a55ead36b01"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-25-5","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":25,"verse":5,"english":"And in the interests of Brāhmaṇas, kine, and celestials, I am ready to act as desired by you of immeasurable energy.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.763,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-26-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1025005","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8561ed3c8d1431c1096dcdd3c619b6ca55e4aad86cb123471dac0f4a8ae895f3","compact":"01710d9234b894c3bebfaf46b3da851f9898eeb91c5c1fcacdf2d43cdb6b5b68","nasal":"01710d9234b894c3bebfaf46b3da851f9898eeb91c5c1fcacdf2d43cdb6b5b68"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-25-6","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":25,"verse":6,"english":"Having said this, that repressor of foes, with clenched fist, twanged his bow-string, filling the ten cardinal points with the sounds. And at those sounds, the dwellers in Tāțakā's forest were filled with perturbation, and Tātakā also amazed at those sounds, became exceedingly wroth.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.638,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-26-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1025006","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3b42d4923d44e376a22ee850a236c0dd2604a55640ddbbc06ced5513c874bd1e","compact":"63e994155d7d0babea4fd40136fea4553ea3f5b69612986acef130ef61b9cb29","nasal":"63e994155d7d0babea4fd40136fea4553ea3f5b69612986acef130ef61b9cb29"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-25-7","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":25,"verse":7,"english":"Having said this, that repressor of foes, with clenched fist, twanged his bow-string, filling the ten cardinal points with the sounds. And at those sounds, the dwellers in Tāțakā's forest were filled with perturbation, and Tātakā also amazed at those sounds, became exceedingly wroth.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.831,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-26-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1025007","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e7631194289547b16ba57c65020643fec8b6f07b78b23acef69bd84bd7e519ba","compact":"bf0a1c49f869b0a9b973e2f68a46e47df7aae977137083c129b326ed4b799ea9","nasal":"bf0a1c49f869b0a9b973e2f68a46e47df7aae977137083c129b326ed4b799ea9"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-25-8","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":25,"verse":8,"english":"And rendered almost insensible by anger, that Räksasī furiously rushed in a main towards the spot whence had come the report.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.746,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-26-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1025008","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6bf2cbc395fe958e6dac0c82415a33e9b60d19131cb3e6f7ca47f80a7d71977a","compact":"f06bdc3063fb952a26cae8c60955d97baddccaeacac2c374ce22a4d0ae272c84","nasal":"f06bdc3063fb952a26cae8c60955d97baddccaeacac2c374ce22a4d0ae272c84"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-25-9","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":25,"verse":9,"english":"And beholding that frightful one of hideous visage and colossal proportions, transported with rage, Raghu's descendant spoke to Laksmana,9","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.889,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-26-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1025009","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"02cb0212f9988c88439091a8833b2e22054d2e23c1e10f7f0f0f3f97e28e2207","compact":"2e87636ec5ed9ad8547a7e347233dbf9cc8790ab035fa48b237c15f52564939d","nasal":"264133fdd95c70773e43bcc8f0907b5ed8c806cfe52edbc8bd9b8639d897368f"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-25-10","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":25,"verse":10,"english":"Behold, O Laksmana, the terrible and hideous body of yonder Yakṣiṇī! The sight of her strike terror into the hearts of even the brave.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-26-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1025010","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"263a8779978055dae5ef1891605b4fd7d6d3dfd2d6537a7288beb77cba5b506d","compact":"e67b447612e383955ee1f9c86cc10eff5c12aadc2a64b41d6a852eb8d4decd59","nasal":"26ce85a445d9cc08026b56bb1963994f0a54b83e1720fced8a0e4f948c72e083"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-25-11","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":25,"verse":11,"english":"Mark! This irrepressible one, possessing all the resources of illusion, will I oppose, and deprive her of ears and nose.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.818,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-26-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1025011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fde853345d2eac74f19dd085b01dccd00041e2e8847b6419b3fcd0d008e05ac6","compact":"9ca3c47f8624c995ae0c289f8a4a752b7e84eb8126d05d40c309bc0f0788e061","nasal":"9ca3c47f8624c995ae0c289f8a4a752b7e84eb8126d05d40c309bc0f0788e061"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-25-12","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":25,"verse":12,"english":"But I dare not slay her, she being protected by virtue of her feminineness. I intend only to oppose her course, and deprive her of her prowess.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.726,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-26-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1025012","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8260be1be19958810020fcaeb772d2d547ff102b4e1c77a7c9ef9bda0260ea9d","compact":"c6b3270986e135200bf20247994bf31ae89ba5a9cfaa35891eb0c6e2df2e8a12","nasal":"b7ad32b6eccbbc83f41428c427e81ba9d8f969f7075f983c6037f0e23bc0b24c"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-25-13","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":25,"verse":13,"english":"As Rāma was speaking thus, Tāțakā, deprived of sense through ire, uttering roars, with uplifted arms rushed against him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.77,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-26-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1025013","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d5016852c4cd8c316d351200305ca120af69906babd7ebd6ddbc07c2a9c11567","compact":"7c81ff73cbf8e5cf3471c4013c44fb786ca535fd3901cdd2dcb446fcb0300fc9","nasal":"421fcd24962fbdf9f16d7d65ec88e81ff63abca31fd465b736f0689587c804ca"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-25-14","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":25,"verse":14,"english":"Being thus hemmed in with a network of shafts, she possessed of the powers of illusion, rushed against Kākutstha and Lakşmaņa, uttering terrible roars. And as that Yaksi, in prowess like to a thunder-bolt, was rushing on, Rāma pierced her chest with arrows, and thereat she dropped down and died.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.846,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-26-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1025014","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f1c0e9cc2366dd97f01eda9890e6ea261cc4090a4eb17c9a5cd479da11846794","compact":"be311b01bf0a3f3d1bac8d8819c9cd95a88023c1923a39ad3de245cff485d3d3","nasal":"4bd9e486f4e121543143a96489835d4b24e3d6b4333dd279d19e83c0dee176ff"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-25-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":25,"verse":15,"english":"Upon seeing that grim-visaged one slain, the lord of the celestials together with the celestials themselves honouring Kākutstha, exclaimed Well, Well!.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-26-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1025015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c8863e335fec84e80b8229f6c6a3024fdc41a9f075959a6a0d310f070d8d2a63","compact":"a809d16035d3caf57e270ee5547268724fc894bc3f39a8b8d3877915e7e491c3","nasal":"a809d16035d3caf57e270ee5547268724fc894bc3f39a8b8d3877915e7e491c3"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-25-16","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":25,"verse":16,"english":"And exceedingly pleased, the thousand-eyed Purandara, together with the delighted deities, said to Viśvāmitra.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-26-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1025016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a7fcfa63190e4a0c1aaa9630bb90f06cdb6a829338a9ae7280131083798ed99b","compact":"6518d299e36fbb8682df49e882c0e5338d0686730a4609c8d3ee153d6d58b1b0","nasal":"6518d299e36fbb8682df49e882c0e5338d0686730a4609c8d3ee153d6d58b1b0"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-25-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":25,"verse":17,"english":"O ascetic, O Kusika's son, good betide you! all the Maruts with Indra at their head, have been gratified with this act (of Rāma's). Do you, O Brāhmaṇa, confer upon Raghu's descendant the sons of Prajāpati Kțśāśva, of true prowess, and charged with ascetic energy.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-26-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1025017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1ba1e6ba2d2af31396216e163f2c505bbd1ff609e36be0e231d67da41449e959","compact":"ffc8299e4fc9f7f1594a3ffcf01ec9157a2f1e9163f68705790b271fad1aea1c","nasal":"81f35a4898d0f396ccc4b38ac0d65117cc655d230dce15556199b135e0159687"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-25-18","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":25,"verse":18,"english":"O ascetic, O Kusika's son, good betide you! all the Maruts with Indra at their head, have been gratified with this act (of Rāma's). Do you, O Brāhmaṇa, confer upon Raghu's descendant the sons of Prajāpati Kțśāśva, of true prowess, and charged with ascetic energy.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.712,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-26-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1025018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"40fdacbbda606f266d3e6147fab66c24cf68cd849c08fab52011d4d1a474619a","compact":"1f256d869713b03fb040a98d28ae4036f27455c3a6af55177e48d48900592fe6","nasal":"01cc9beefc223d3d8603589b69ae6765bb1b716c2141516506206f630d3309de"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-25-19","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":25,"verse":19,"english":"And ever following you, he, O Brāhmaṇa, is fit to receive them of you. And this son of the king is to accomplish a mighty task in the interests of the celestials.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.59,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs"